{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>This is the book of the generations of Adam</b> — the sons whom he will mention in the section. And in my opinion, it alludes to the entire Torah, for the entire Torah is a book of the generations of Adam. Therefore it says here \"a book\" (סֵפֶר) and does not say \"and these are the generations of Adam\" (וְאֵלֶּה תּוֹלְדוֹת אָדָם) as it says in other places: (Genesis 25:12) \"and these are the generations of Ishmael,\" \"and these are the generations of Isaac\" (v. 19), and so all of them. And the meaning of \"in the day that Elohim created Adam\" is connected to what precedes it, for he will begin with Adam himself — he will mention concerning him that he was created from nothing, and therefore it says, in the day that Elohim created from nothing this Adam who is mentioned, in the likeness of Elohim He made him — he will explain that he is the work of Elohim and in the likeness of Elohim. And he mentioned that just as He created him from nothing, so too He created his wife, and he said:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:45.503509625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}